From 7fff05c665fe4430c8d3633bc946fc7213ae78b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:48:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(motion): re-centre a pole axis only on an isotropic
 part, by area

Review of PR #204: a 100 x 100 x 10 plate with a turned r5 boss at
(20, 20) read as a trusted (0.667, 0.667, 0.333) axis. The trimmed half
was taken by facet count (the boss is 792 of 804 facets, 1.3 % of the
area), and the plate's two-triangle faces put every normal line through
its centre, which any line through it meets.

The least-trimmed-squares re-centring now takes the AREA-weighted
median, requires the kept half to carry MIN_KEPT_SHARE of the answering
area on MIN_KEPT facets (as axis_robust::reweigh does), and runs only
when the normal moment is isotropic. Elsewhere the plain line's drag
stays the evidence, as it was on main.

Pinned by a_plate_with_an_off_centre_boss_is_refused_by_name.

Refs #152

