From e883ae67b158cddd2361ff6968eb65c4864cb7cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:29:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(motion): judge each pencil of normal lines alone;
 only inliers vouch for roundness

Review of PR #223 found two more trusted wrong axes from the #208
mechanism:
- B1: a prism whose sides are split into 3+ rectangles along its length
  (square bar, stepped block, stacked cubes) with an off-centre boss read
  Z through the prism's centre. No one point held half the inliers, so
  the pencil guard never fired, and the coarseness gate counted the
  boss's bearings although the boss misses the axis.
- B2: crossed single-band cylinders read the cross axis: the Z rod's
  wall is a pencil at the origin that "meets" Y, and its union with the
  Y rod's ring looked round.

The coarseness gate now reads only the facets that meet the axis. The
inliers are peeled into pencils (lines through one point, one after
another), and each pencil is judged by itself: its area-weighted
trigonometric moments k = 1..4 about the axis must vanish (a revolve's
ring is even; a crossing rod piles its share on two bearings, a box on
four). The sum, weighted by pencil area, may be at most 10 % of the
inlier area. A shallow single-band D-flat still reads its axis.

Pins (each fails on 2fe41a2):
a_square_bar_split_along_its_length_with_a_boss_is_refused_by_name,
stepped_and_stacked_blocks_with_a_boss_are_refused_by_name,
crossed_cylinders_never_read_the_cross_axis;
a_single_band_shaft_with_a_shallow_flat_still_reads_its_axis guards
the D-flat.

Fixes #208

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
